questions.statementEn:
Assume installed requests, configured environment credentials and a trusted device TLS certificate. HTTP200 returns exactly the JSON below (enabled is omitted for Loopback0). What does the script do for Gi0/1, whose administrative enabled leaf is explicitly false?

```python
import os
import requests

url = "https://192.168.1.1/restconf/data/ietf-interfaces:interfaces"
headers = {"Accept": "application/yang-data+json"}
response = requests.get(url, headers=headers,
    auth=(os.environ["CCNA_USER"], os.environ["CCNA_PASSWORD"]),
    verify=True, timeout=10)
response.raise_for_status()
for intf in response.json()["ietf-interfaces:interfaces"]["interface"]:
    if intf.get("enabled") is True:
        print(f"Administratively enabled: {intf['name']} - Type: {intf['type']}")
```
```json
{
  "ietf-interfaces:interfaces": {
    "interface": [
      {
        "name": "Gi0/1",
        "type": "iana-if-type:ethernetCsmacd",
        "enabled": false
      },
      {
        "name": "Gi0/2",
        "type": "iana-if-type:ethernetCsmacd",
        "enabled": true
      },
      {
        "name": "Loopback0",
        "type": "iana-if-type:softwareLoopback"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

